	<item>
		<title>AEW Dynamite Results – 11/25/26 (Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite: Continental Classic and more!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398347-aew-dynamite-results-11-25-26-thanksgiving-eve-dynamite-continental-classic-and-more/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398347-aew-dynamite-results-11-25-26-thanksgiving-eve-dynamite-continental-classic-and-more/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:00:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW Dynamite Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/25/26 AEW Dynamite results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Continental Classic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398347</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite ResultsNovember 25, 2026Ralston (Omaha), Nebraska (Liberty First Credit Union Arena)Results by: Alex Kahrs of&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398347-aew-dynamite-results-11-25-26-thanksgiving-eve-dynamite-continental-classic-and-more/">AEW Dynamite Results – 11/25/26 (Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite: Continental Classic and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AEW Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite Results</strong><br><strong>November 25, 2026</strong><br><strong>Ralston (Omaha), Nebraska (Liberty First Credit Union Arena)</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It is Wednesday, my dudes&#8230;you know what that means!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary welcomes us to the show before we go to a video looking back at the first week of the Continental Classic. They address Daniel Garcia being pulled from the tournament after sustaining an injury in his match, with Konosuke Takeshita taking his place at a slight disadvantage as he inherits the 0 points earned going into week two. From there, we get some hype for the matches for tonight before heading to ringside for our opening contest!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out first is Orange Cassidy, followed by &#8220;Speedball&#8221; Mike Bailey to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-gold-league-match-orange-cassidy-3-vs-speedball-mike-bailey-0" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Gold League Match: Orange Cassidy (3) vs. ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey (0)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Code of Honor (handshake) adhered to before the two lock up. Bailey with an arm wringer, but it&#8217;s countered by Cassidy&#8230;only for Speedball to cartwheel out of it for an arm drag of sorts. He takes Cassidy down, but Orange takes control for a nearfall. They trade offense until Bailey gets Cassidy down for a nearfall, catching Orange by surprise for a backslide that gets a second two count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy rolls out of the ring for a breather, returning to lock up with Bailey. The two trade holds once more, leading to an exchange of nearfalls. Orange traps Bailey by the leg, getting a very close two count before Speedball escapes to the outside. Bailey back in the ring, evading an Orange Punch for a kick to the midsection. Cassidy fires back, landing some chops to the chest. Mike goes for a kick but gets caught with a backbreaker by Orange instead, and Cassidy maintains control with a low dropkick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fight leaves the ring as Cassidy gets caught with a hard kick, followed by an Asai moonsault by Speedball sending him to the floor. Bailey brings Orange back in the ring for a missile dropkick, and a cover leads to a two count&#8230;and a cross arm breaker by Speedball! Cassidy gets to the ropes for a break, leaving the ring as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy in the corner now, sending Bailey&#8217;s head into the turnbuckle to regain control. He follows up with some right hands to the head of Speedball, only to take a hard kick as ten minutes remain in the bout. Bailey sends Orange to the apron for a backflip knee drop, but lands on the hardest part of the ring as Cassidy dodges it. He sends Speedball to the floor before going for a dive, but as Speedball is sent to the floor he catches Cassidy with a cross arm breaker!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bailey gets back for another knee drop but once again it comes up shy, allowing Cassidy to send him into the ring. He goes for an ankle lock, but Speedball kicks his way out of the hold. Orange hits the ropes and lands a DDT for a nearfall. Orange Punch is evaded as Bailey lands a knee strike. Cassidy tries to block a crane kick but gets sent to the mat by Speedball, who ends up taking a Beach Break to the canvas&#8230;only to kick out at two on the cover that follows.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy fires up, trying to take Bailey down for a three count but to no avail. He goes for an Orange Punch, but runs into a spinning roundhouse kick by Speedball&#8230;who gets the pin for his first three points!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-speedball-mike-bailey-3" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bailey celebrates as we take a look at the other matches for the tournament happening tonight. From there, we go to a video package looking at Adam Copeland, who is trying to figure himself out in what will be his final year of wrestling.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Backstage, Don Callis talks about the situation with Cope fighting a bear prior to Full Gear, noting that he still couldn&#8217;t take down Okada&#8230;who emphasizes this with a quick ranking. Callis says that Copeland is officially retired after failing to beat the Rainmaker for the title, and will hold a &#8220;retirement ceremony&#8221; for him next week. He walks off as Okada lets us know he is thankful&#8230;family!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Backstage we hear from the Brawling Birds, who have their eye on the Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Championship match later tonight. They promise that the United Empire will be back in full force soon, and Dynamite rolls on as we head back to ringside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jon Moxley makes his entrance for our next Continental Classic bout, making his way through the crowd as the crowd cheers him on. We get a promo from Kevin Knight after Collision, with The Jet looking ahead to his bout against Mox after defeating Ciampa. Speaking of The Jet, out comes Kevin Knight as we get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-gold-league-match-jon-moxley-0-vs-kevin-knight-3" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Gold League Match: Jon Moxley (0) vs. Kevin Knight (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mox looks for the upper hand as he backs Knight into the corner, and The Jet leaves the ring for a breather. He comes back in, but is caught by the champ&#8230;who brings Kevin to the mat for a nearfall. Knight counters out of an arm wringer, but takes a chop sending him to the mat. Knight leaves the ring again, and Mox tries to draw him in by laying on the mat&#8230;only to rise up as The Jet starts to get back in.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Knight thinks better of this, and we reset with a side headlock by Mox who takes his opponent to the canvas. He goes to work on Knight until The Jet manages to escape to the outside, finally drawing the champ out to follow him&#8230;where Kevin intercepts him! Mox back up as he and Knight trade strikes. Knight sent to the corner now as Mox lands some more shots.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kevin manages to fight back, bringing the champ to the outside where he lays in some shots of his own before bringing Mox back into the ring. He mocks the crowd as he gets onto the apron&#8230;only to be sent back down with a dropkick by Moxley, who then sends him into the barricade with a dive through the ropes!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He brings Kevin around the ring, looking to send him into the ring post. Knight counters, and sends the champ into the ring steps before mocking the crowd again as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Knight with a nearfall as we come back, and he goes after the arm of Moxley. Jon fights to his feet for a chop, forcing Kevin to the ropes. Knight catches the champ with a sleeper hold transitioned into a rear naked choke. Mox drops to the mat as ten minutes remain, but Jon fights back to his feet. He connects with a piledriver sending The Jet down hard to the mat.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He brings Kevin to the corner for some punches before going for a right hand. Knight blocks it, but takes a cutter by the champ instead. The fight ends up in the corner once more as Knight sends Mox into the turnbuckle, rolling him up for two. He goes to the ropes but gets caught with a double underhook, but The Jet breaks free. The two men trade strikes until Mox goes to the ropes, only to walk into a kick by Knight who lands a DDT for a nearfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Crash Landing connects, but The Jet only gets a two count. Double wristlock by Kevin, but Mox manages to get back to his feet. Knight continues to go to work on the arm, forcing the champ to the mat. He goes up top, but Mox rolls out of the way&#8230;before landing a King Kong lariat for two! Knight counters for a nearfall of his own as five minutes remain.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fight gets to the apron as Mox goes for a stomp, but Knight dodges before driving the champ&#8217;s head onto the hardest part of the ring. He goes up top but has to readjust to not fall onto the boot of Mox. He clutches Mox deep for a two count, and an argument with the ref after allows Mox to trap him with a choke. Knight breaks free but the champ transitions to a cross arm breaker&#8230;and this forces The Jet to tap out!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-submission-jon-moxley-3" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via submission: Jon Moxley (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mox celebrates while Knight regroups on the ramp, as commentary talks about the five-way tie for the lead in the Gold League. From there we go to a video package looking at Konosuke Takeshita stepping into the Continental Classic with a disadvantage&#8230;but as someone who has nearly gone the distance in the past, he still has a chance to pull off a big win this year!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We hear from Brodido and Adam Page ahead of their respective Continental Classic matches, with Brody King and Bandido both up with 3 points in the Blue League. They each talk about their opponents, with Hangman looking to prove himself with his first 3 points in the tournament as Dynamite rolls on.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We head back to ringside for&#8230;an 18-Man Tag Match? Oh boy.</p>



<h3 id="18-man-tag-match-the-don-callis-family-vs-local-talents-out-the-wazoo" class="wp-block-heading">18-Man Tag Match: The Don Callis Family vs. Local Talents Out The Wazoo</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m not even sure how to recap this match, other than the Family quickly put the beatdown on their opponents. Everyone on Don Callis&#8217;s team gets a time to shine, with Josh Alexander ultimately getting the submission victory.</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-submission-the-don-callis-family" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via submission: The Don Callis Family</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is, of course, all a setup for Don Callis to cut a promo after as he talks about his Don Callis Family Title Initiative as well as Fletcher looking to beat Andrade El Idolo later tonight. The conversation turns to the World Trios Championship, which brings out the Dangerous New Level. Creed says they&#8217;re out here to return the favor after they were interrupted last week.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kofi addresses Austin not fulfilling the dress code (so to speak) before they run down Don for not really giving his family all that much. Since he&#8217;s a bad father, the champs will be the fathers that step up, with Swerve offering a title shot to any of the three &#8220;idiots&#8221; in the Family for Thanksgiving Collision. Josh speaks up, talking about how he and his Canadian and Mexican friends and Family members don&#8217;t even celebrate American Thanksgiving (including Rocky Romero, who Creed remarks is actually from LA), before accepting the challenge for tomorrow night.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We head backstage, where Big Stoke talks about what he&#8217;s thankful for, including FTR and the Kasper Brothers. We&#8217;ll see the latter in action tomorrow night, and FTR teaming with them for Winter is Coming against Motor City Machine Guns.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kasper Bros strongly suggest they have that match next week before walking off, and we head back to ringside for our next match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before we get that match, however, out comes The Cut (as I wonder why we have so many cowboys in AEW), with Mercedes Moné out here as well to introduce Jay White after addressing AZM attacking her last week. Jay congratulates Mox on finally getting on the board but promises to be the winner of this tournament, before talking down Hangman Adam Page.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page makes his entrance as The Cut and Moné leave ringside per the rules of the tournament, and we get this match underway.</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-blue-league-match-jay-white-3-vs-hangman-adam-page-0" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Blue League Match: Jay White (3) vs. Hangman Adam Page (0)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">White gives the Hangman a hug, welcoming him to the Continental Classic before the two men lock up. Page breaks free of the Switchblade&#8217;s grip, looking for a side headlock. Jay counters with one of his own before being sent to the ropes for a shoulder tackle. Jay fights back, sending Hangman down with a knee strike before mocking him with a nod to Swerve Strickland.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This riles up Page, who sends White out of the ring before following him for some further shots. Jay fights back before being sent into a guardrail by Page as the ref makes the count. The two return to the ring at the count of five, with Page taking Jay down with a fall away slam and a chop. He follows up with a big side slam, but it&#8217;s only good for two as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay back in control as he goes after the neck of Page. He fights off a powerbomb attempt by the Hangman, but Adam holds on for a Liger Bomb and a nearfall. White fights back, sending Page to the mat with a suplex. He goes after the injured nose of Hangman, who breaks free before pummeling White with some forearm strikes to the ropes. Ten minutes remain as the two end up trading strikes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay gets knocked down as Page goes to the ropes for a Buckshot Lariat. White is back on his feet, mocking him to give it a shot. He goes in for a legwhip but gets bitten by Page, sending him to the canvas&#8230;but the Hangman gets caught with a Saito suplex over the ropes, landing on the apron before falling to the floor. Ref with the count, before Jay leaves the ring for a Blade Runner&#8230;only to be dropped to the floor with a Dead Eye! Page brings him back into the ring, but White drops down to stop him from going for a Buckshot.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page gets back in the ring, looking for another Dead Eye&#8230;but White evades it, setting up for a Cutthroat Suplex instead! Page is back up already, taking him down with a lariat before following up with the Buckshot&#8230;only for White to roll out of the ring for safety. Ref with the count as Page leaves to bring Switchblade back into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page gets back in as well, only to be dropped with another Cutthroat Suplex. Jay looks for a Blade Runner, but takes one from Page instead. White ducks a Buckshot attempt, dropping the Hangman with a Blade Runner to keep him down for the win!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-jay-white-6" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: Jay White (6)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay celebrates as we head backstage, where we hear from Mina Shirakawa and Queen Aminata&#8230;but not for long, as they are interrupted by Athena and Billie Starkz. Athena gives the Queen some props but tells her to leave her minions alone, and this all leads to a match set for Thanksgiving Collision and Aminata and Mina face Athena and Starkz as we go to commercial.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Refresh for the latest results!</em></p>



<h3 id="quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Continental Classic Gold League Match:</strong> ‘Speedball’ Mike Bailey (3) def. Orange Cassidy (3)</li>



<li><strong>Continental Classic Gold League Match:</strong> Jon Moxley (3) def. Kevin Knight (3)</li>



<li><strong>18-Man Tag Match:</strong> The Don Callis Family def. Local Talents Out The Wazoo</li>



<li><strong>Continental Classic Blue League Match:</strong> Jay White (6) def. Hangman Adam Page (0)</li>
</ul>



<h3 id="still-to-come" class="wp-block-heading">Still to Come:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>AEW Women’s World Tag Team Championship Match:</strong> Wrathlander (Kris Statlander and Harley Cameron defends against Divine Dominion (Megan Bayne and Lena Kross)</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Andrade El Idolo vs. Kyle Fletcher</li>



<li>AEW World Trios Champions The Dangerous New Level to appear</li>



<li>MJF to appear</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398347-aew-dynamite-results-11-25-26-thanksgiving-eve-dynamite-continental-classic-and-more/">AEW Dynamite Results – 11/25/26 (Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite: Continental Classic and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
