			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Taya Valkyrie addresses decision to leave AEW</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398334-taya-valkyrie-addresses-decision-to-leave-aew/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398334-taya-valkyrie-addresses-decision-to-leave-aew/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:34:22 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ROH]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Taya Valkyrie]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398334</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with TMZ Sports, Taya Valkyrie talked about her decision to decline an offer for an&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398334-taya-valkyrie-addresses-decision-to-leave-aew/">Taya Valkyrie addresses decision to leave AEW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with TMZ Sports, Taya Valkyrie talked about her decision to decline an offer for an AEW contract extension.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Valkyrie had not competed for the company since an ROH taping in January, which turned out to be related to a previously undisclosed injury.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On finally being cleared, only to reach a crossroads with her career in the company:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I was dealing with an injury most of this year, earlier in the year, which I then got cleared from, which I also didn’t really talk about because I just don’t feel like that’s something that everybody needs to know about. And AEW was super supportive, helped me get through that. Got cleared, feel amazing, all these things. And then, yeah, it just kind of came down to the decision of, like, do I want to stay here or do I not? And I really had to look at myself and be like, okay, what do I want?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I’ve been working so hard for so long, and I just really have always bet on myself. I’ve always been probably someone that they’re like, ‘What the f–k is she doing that for?’ But guess what? I bet on myself, and I also put in the work. A lot of people are like, ‘What have you been doing? I don’t get it.’ And I’m like, ‘I’ve been doing so much that people don’t see so that when these kinds of situations happen, I’m ready to go.’</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I just really felt like I wanted more from the company and wanted more for myself, especially after 16 years in the business. If it’s not a good fit anymore, it’s not a good fit. So I have nothing bad to say about anybody. Love Tony Khan, love everyone there, but I just felt like it was my time.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During her run with AEW, Valkyrie worked on such concepts as Making Towns and Johnny Loves Taya, and she notes she was &#8220;constantly coming up with ideas and costumes,&#8221; noting that her ideas not sticking led her to feel she had to &#8220;go somewhere else to be happy and find that creativity,&#8221; adding:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At some point, you’re just like, okay, well, maybe I don’t fit here anymore. Maybe they don’t necessarily think that I am what they need or whatever. And that’s fine, but you have to be okay with deciding that. And I just kind of made that decision for myself. I want to be creative. I’m not done. And I don’t like people trying to think for me or telling me that I need to be in this box over here.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/aew/taya-valkyrie-explains-why-she-left-aew/">F4WOnline</a></p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="Taya Valkyrie Reveals Why She Left AEW | Inside The Ring" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/9Qy-FJet2XA?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398334-taya-valkyrie-addresses-decision-to-leave-aew/">Taya Valkyrie addresses decision to leave AEW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398334-taya-valkyrie-addresses-decision-to-leave-aew/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: Another tag team in AEW nearing the end of their current contracts</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398328-report-another-tag-team-in-aew-nearing-the-end-of-their-current-contracts/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398328-report-another-tag-team-in-aew-nearing-the-end-of-their-current-contracts/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:24:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[contracts]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[The Righeous]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398328</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider is reporting that The Righteous (Vincent and Dutch) are nearing the end of their current contracts with&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398328-report-another-tag-team-in-aew-nearing-the-end-of-their-current-contracts/">Report: Another tag team in AEW nearing the end of their current contracts</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/article/214021/another-set-of-tna-talents-coming-due-on-contracts.html?p=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PWInsider is reporting</a> that The Righteous (Vincent and Dutch) are nearing the end of their current contracts with TNA Wrestling.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes it is believed The Righteous&#8217; contracts expire on December 31, 2026. It is also being said Vincent and Dutch are currently in discussions with TNA for new deals, but nothing has been agreed upon.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Righteous signed with TNA this past January, after their contracts with AEW expired. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Hardys, Xia Brookside and Rich Swann are all going to be free agents at the end of this year, if no new contracts with TNA are agreed upon. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During the November 5 episode of IMPACT, Brookside turned on Harley Hudson and joined The Righteous. </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398328-report-another-tag-team-in-aew-nearing-the-end-of-their-current-contracts/">Report: Another tag team in AEW nearing the end of their current contracts</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398328-report-another-tag-team-in-aew-nearing-the-end-of-their-current-contracts/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
