		<item>
		<title>Cody Rhodes looks back on involvement with John Cena&#8217;s retirement run</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398322-cody-rhodes-looks-back-on-involvement-with-john-cenas-retirement-run/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398322-cody-rhodes-looks-back-on-involvement-with-john-cenas-retirement-run/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:50:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cody Rhodes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SummerSlam]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Undisputed WWE Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WrestleMania 41]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398322</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with 7PM in Brooklyn with Carmelo Anthony, a Wave Original, Cody Rhodes talked about his&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398322-cody-rhodes-looks-back-on-involvement-with-john-cenas-retirement-run/">Cody Rhodes looks back on involvement with John Cena&#8217;s retirement run</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@7PMinBrooklyn">7PM in Brooklyn with Carmelo Anthony</a>, a Wave Original, Cody Rhodes talked about his involvement with John Cena&#8217;s farewell run in 2025.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Speaking with the NBA legend and co-host Kazeem Famuyide, the former Undisputed WWE Champion reflected on night Cena turned heel at Elimination Chamber, leading to their showdown at WrestleMania 41:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I knew John turning heel or turning in general or doing something that they didn&#8217;t expect was going to be a big discussion point, a talking point… But John loaded and peppered that with things. Prime example – his face on the hug and the Rock, you know, the across the throat and the sign language that was happening unbeknownst to me. Travis. And then with the slap as well. It&#8217;s chaotic as hell. It was one in a moment nutshell type thing because then John and I would not have those players as we move forward in Wrestlemania. But I wouldn&#8217;t change a thing.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rhodes dropped the title to Cena on that night, leading to a rematch at SummerSlam that saw the American Nightmare become a two-time champion and Cena attempting to redeem himself.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On the pressure of facing Cena in that stretch of the year, Rhodes stated:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I learned so much from John… I learned something about myself in the role I was in, you know, the whole kind of QB1 element of it developing. The thing I learned about myself is the same thing that other people in my spot learned is I have to survive this more than anything. They love him. He is going to his last Wrestlemania with me, his last SummerSlam with me. I&#8217;m taking the title off of him. He&#8217;s breaking the record with me. I just have to be able to survive this on the other side. So feel free if you need to boo me or besmirch my name or come for me. That felt like the opportunity where that&#8217;s what&#8217;s supposed to happen. The pressure is on.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the full interview, Rhodes also discussed Travis Scott bursting his eardrum, his complicated relationship with The Rock, and much more.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="Cody Rhodes on The Rock Demanding His SOUL, Roman Reigns &amp; the Pressure of Being WWE&amp;apos;s Top Guy" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/kaFeS5sqAms?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398322-cody-rhodes-looks-back-on-involvement-with-john-cenas-retirement-run/">Cody Rhodes looks back on involvement with John Cena&#8217;s retirement run</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398322-cody-rhodes-looks-back-on-involvement-with-john-cenas-retirement-run/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
